cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool, please cite it as below."
title: "AI Act Compliance Helper"
abstract: >-
  Classification tool for Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 laying down harmonised rules on artificial
  intelligence (Artificial Intelligence Act) and for Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data
  Protection Regulation), in German and English. Users answer a question flow taken from the
  draft Commission guidelines of 19 May 2026 on high-risk AI systems and receive the risk class
  with the exact provision it rests on, plus the obligations per role. The classification is
  computed deterministically from plain-text rule files, not by a language model; a language model
  at most phrases the fixed result. Measured against the Commission's official examples, 207 of
  217 are classified as the Commission does. Full-text search over the legal corpus combines
  four retrieval routes by reciprocal rank fusion and runs with local embedding models, without
  a key for any external service and without network access. Not legal advice.
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-09'
